#====================================================================
# Draft: kpackage 6.18.0.2 consuming karchive/6.19.0 - CMake dependency
#        discovery (find_dependency(ZLIB)) repair (recipe layer)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-KPACKAGE-KARCHIVE-619-ZLIB-DISCOVERY
trigger_tool:           conan|cmake|kpackage|karchive|FindZLIB|CMakeDeps|pkg-config
phase:                  dependency-resolution|packaging|testing
error_signature:        Could NOT find ZLIB|missing: ZLIB_LIBRARY ZLIB_INCLUDE_DIR|find_dependency\(ZLIB\)|KF6ArchiveConfig\.cmake

severity:               2
category:               conan-recipe-dependency-graph
match_keywords:         kpackage, karchive, 6.19.0, 6.18.0.2, KF6ArchiveConfig, find_dependency, ZLIB, zlib/1.3.1.1, OpenSSL, openssl/3.5.6.1, zstd, PKG_CONFIG_PATH, conan_cmakedeps_paths.cmake

title:                  kpackage/6.18.0.2 consuming karchive/6.19.0 fails KF6ArchiveConfig find_dependency(ZLIB) unless transitive zlib/OpenSSL/zstd paths are injected by the recipe

root_cause:             The published karchive/6.19.0 binary exports KF6ArchiveConfig.cmake which unconditionally runs find_dependency(ZLIB), find_dependency(OpenSSL) and pkg_check_modules(LibZstd); its KF6ArchiveTargets INTERFACE_LINK_LIBRARIES carries $<LINK_ONLY:ZLIB::ZLIB>, $<LINK_ONLY:OpenSSL::Crypto> and $<LINK_ONLY:PkgConfig::LibZstd>. A consumer recipe whose hand-written conan_cmakedeps_paths.cmake only exposes the direct KF deps (karchive/kcoreaddons/ki18n) never makes the transitive zlib/1.3.1.1, openssl and zstd packages discoverable to FindZLIB/FindOpenSSL/pkg-config, so configure fails with "Could NOT find ZLIB (missing: ZLIB_LIBRARY ZLIB_INCLUDE_DIR)".
affected_scope:         Any KF6-conanfile consumer that consumes the static karchive/6.19.0 export and relies on a manual CMake path layer instead of CMakeDeps propagation; kpackage/6.18.0.2 is the delivered instance.
verification_cmd:       conan create archives/k/kpackage/6.18.0.2 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           recipe-layer-transitive-dependency-path-injection
rec_description:        In the consumer conanfile.py generate(): (1) require the direct dep karchive/6.19.0 and also openssl/3.5.6.1 so the exported Config's find_dependency(OpenSSL) is satisfiable; (2) prepend the transitive zlib/1.3.1.1 and openssl package root/lib/cmake/include into the generated conan_cmakedeps_paths.cmake (declared dependency metadata, not hard-coded cache paths); (3) prepend the transitive zstd lib/pkgconfig dir onto ENV{PKG_CONFIG_PATH} (set(ENV...) prepend); (4) since karchive/6.19.0 is a static library linked by bare -lKF6Archive and its LINK_ONLY transitive libs never reach the link line, add -L<zlib/zstd libdir> -lz -lzstd to CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS and CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS. Preserve R05/R07 relocatability (no .conan2/.cache path in DT_NEEDED/RPATH/RUNPATH).
rec_command:            conan create archives/k/kpackage/6.18.0.2 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conanfile.py requirements()/generate() in archives/k/kpackage/6.18.0.2/

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      upgrade-to-cmakefiledeps-propagation
fallback_description:   Replace the hand-written conan_cmakedeps_paths.cmake layer with full CMakeDeps generation for the KF deps (where their cmake_find_mode allows), letting find_dependency(ZLIB/OpenSSL/LibZstd) resolve through generated configs instead of manual path injection.
fallback_command:       conan install --requires=kpackage/6.18.0.2 -g CMakeDeps -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       use --build=missing to substitute the karchive graph|use a system ZLIB|use a lockfile/version override as evidence|inject hard-coded producer-cache paths|downgrade karchive below 6.19.0
forbid_1_reason:        R36/R37 and the task verification mode require a clean dependency graph resolved from the registry with the exact references (karchive/6.19.0, zlib/1.3.1.1); cache/solver bypasses would mask the real discovery failure and produce non-reproducible artifacts.
forbid_1_consequence:   Unverifiable/irreproducible graph, CI L0j same-version rejection, or a non-relocatable artifact with machine-private paths.

principles:             real-evidence-over-assumption, declared-dependency-metadata, minimal-recipe-diff, relocatability-preserving

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
